      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While companies must inform third parties of the deletion request, they generally do not need to verify that every single vendor has successfully deleted its copies, especially if deletion is technically impossible. Instead, legal guidance often allows the controller to rely on make-good measures, such as requesting confirmation or ensuring contractual clauses mandate deletion within a specific timeframe, rather than warranting absolute physical removal. This pragmatic approach respects the scope of the right to be forgotten while remaining proportional to the company's ability to enforce compliance across a network of subprocessors.",
